$\begin{align}
\text{vertex's }x\text{-coordinate}&=\dfrac{(\goldD{-9})+(\goldD{-8})}{2}
\\\\
&=\blueD{-\dfrac{17}{2}}
\end{align}$

Now we can find the vertex's $y$-coordinate by evaluating $g\left(\blueD{-\dfrac{17}{2}}\right)$:

$\begin{align}
g\left(\blueD{-\dfrac{17}{2}}\right)&=\left(\blueD{-\dfrac{17}{2}}+9\right)\left(\blueD{-\dfrac{17}{2}}+8\right)
\\\\
&=\left(\dfrac12\right)\left(-\dfrac12\right)
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{1}{4}
\end{align}$
